// check: refuse E_EffectMismatch
// CROWN — latency rides the DEFAULT PARAMETER VALUE. A default is not a
// call-site convenience: SYNTAX desugars it once at the declaration to a
// callee-scoped fill, evaluated in the CALLEE's parameter scope. So the
// default's row is the callee's row, and a caller under `with !E` must
// meet it even though the call site mentions neither the parameter nor
// the effect. Expect E_EffectMismatch.
//
// This carrier is ORACLE-BLIND: the wheel writes no default-valued
// parameter anywhere (measured — 0 across 29 src modules and 2079 fn
// declarations), so the fixpoint, the census and the micro battery are
// all structurally silent here. Its sound twin is the RED evidence —
// sound-default-transport is this file with the call removed, and it
// accepts.
effect E { op() -> Int }

fn takes(a, b = () => op()) = b()

fn bad() with !E = takes(1)

fn main() = bad()
